According to the Liberalised Remittance Scheme (LRS) guidelines, the limit for remittances by a resident individual has been increased to USD 250,000 per financial year for any permitted current or capital account transaction or a combination of both [rbi:rbi_notifications:9756 / para 2].

The permissible capital account transactions by an individual under LRS include:

i) opening of foreign currency account abroad with a bank [rbi:rbi_notifications:9756 / para 3(i)];
ii) purchase of property abroad [rbi:rbi_notifications:9756 / para 3(ii)];
iii) making investments abroad [rbi:rbi_notifications:9756 / para 3(iii)];
iv) setting up Wholly owned subsidiaries and Joint Ventures abroad [rbi:rbi_notifications:9756 / para 3(iv)];
v) extending loans including loans in Indian Rupees to Non-resident Indians (NRIs) who are relatives as defined in Companies Act, 2013 [rbi:rbi_notifications:9756 / para 3(v)].

Note that the effective date for these changes is June 1, 2015, as per the RBI/2014-15/620 circular.
